course: dictionary
lesson: 5944
title: The chewing muscle
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Your masseter is a muscle in each cheek. It pulls your lower jaw up, so you can close your mouth and chew your food. Put your fingers on your cheek and clench your teeth: you can feel it bulge.
explain: Scientists use the word masseter for this muscle. «The jaw muscle, the masseter, bites very hard for its size» tells you it is very strong for how small it is. The word muscle in this sentence is a clue: the masseter is part of your body that moves.
explain: Lots of science words are long, but you can work them out. Look at the sentence around the word, and check what the clues tell you. When you meet «masseter muscle» in a science book, it means the chewing muscle in the cheek.
fact: The masseter is a muscle in each cheek.
fact: The masseter pulls the lower jaw up, so you can close your mouth and chew.
fact: «The jaw muscle, the masseter, bites very hard for its size.» This means it is very strong for its size.
fact: «The heart is the hardest-working muscle.» Muscles are parts of the body that can move and pull.
fact: You can feel your masseter bulge when you clench your teeth.
exercise: Where is the masseter? | In your big toe | *In your cheek, near your back teeth | In your forehead | In your elbow
exercise: «The jaw muscle, the masseter, bites very hard for its size.» What does this tell you? | It is the same size as the heart | *It is very strong for its size | It is the weakest muscle in the body | It only moves your eyes
exercise: What does the masseter do? | It pumps blood round the body | It pushes the jaw down to open the mouth wide | *It pulls the lower jaw up so you can chew | It moves the big toe
test: Which word is the name of the chewing muscle in the cheek? | Heart | Gluteus | Biceps | *Masseter
test: You can feel the masseter bulge when you do what? | Hold your breath | *Clench your teeth | Wiggle your toes | Blink your eyes
exam: Which sentence about the masseter is true? | *It is a muscle that closes the jaw for chewing | It is a bone in the leg | It only grows in animals | It is in the stomach
